# A torus bifurcation of cycles with a closed-form coefficient. The pair (x1, y1) = z runs
# on the cycle |z| = sqrt(beta), z = r exp(i Om t), with Om = 2 and the period T = pi.
# w = x2 + i y2 obeys w' = (lam + 0.8 i) w - gam |w|^2 w with lam = beta - 1/4 and
# gam = 1 + 0.5 i, so the multipliers are exp((lam +- 0.8 i) T) and the pair crosses the unit
# circle at beta = 1/4 with theta = 0.8 pi. The normal form coefficient is d = -2 gam / T,
# so Re d = -2/pi and Im d = -1/pi. Own model.
par beta=0.2
Om=2
lam=beta-0.25
r2=x2^2+y2^2
x1'=beta*x1-Om*y1-(x1^2+y1^2)*x1
y1'=beta*y1+Om*x1-(x1^2+y1^2)*y1
x2'=lam*x2-0.8*y2-r2*(x2-0.5*y2)
y2'=lam*y2+0.8*x2-r2*(y2+0.5*x2)
init x1=0.45,y1=0,x2=0,y2=0
done
